task: stm-sync-commit-fastpath (an attempt that commits answers pure; the Await is reserved for retry)
agent: okay-42
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/stm-sync-commit-fastpath

why: stm-js-direct-bench (§18d) priced a Read-then-Write transaction at
  ~800 B and 70-90 ns on the JVM, ~300 ns on Node, ~1.5 us on Native,
  in both handlers, and named the Async.await staging of an attempt
  that never parks as the shape to move. Both tl2 and direct run the
  attempt inside `Async.await { k => attempt(tx, k) }` even when it
  commits synchronously. Run the first attempt eagerly; on commit answer
  `pure(a)` (a failure rethrows as the effect's failure would); only a
  RetryNow reaches the Await path, where parking is the point. A/B on
  StmBenchmark *ReadWrite (-prof gc) and BenchStmCross on JS/Native; the
  Modify lanes (already pure via the fast path) are the control. Laws:
  every TestStm* on all platforms, the retry laws especially.
